          <div  class="title-page">
               <p>(E) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">Normal Operation Procedure:</b></p>
              <table cellpadding="2">
                
    <tr>
         <th style="width:6%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="width:68%;">Operation Procedure</th>
            <th style="width:11%;">Action by</th>
            <th style="width:10%;">Check</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>
            Ensure compliance with MGL Life Saving Rules and COP requirements.
            Conduct site specific HIRA.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>2</td>
        <td>
            Inform Emergency control room about commencement of NRO.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>3</td>
        <td>
            Issue work permit for confined space entry for entering steel valve
            chambers.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>4</td>
        <td>
            Check for any potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of V2,
            AG/3 &amp; AG/6 and AG/9 remove if any found.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>5</td>
        <td>
            Close the valve V1 (Size 4”) completely and then allow the Jeevan Auto,
            Mastakar Auto, Parker Brother Auto, Gajanan Auto &amp; Oshiwara Depot
            CNG Station compressors to run till auto tripped at low suction pressure.
            Then after allowing DRS 12 to run till 6 bar inlet pressure and then
            close DRS both stream inlet valve of DRS 12.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>6</td>
        <td>
            Connect vent stack and flame arrestor at Valve AG/3, AG/6 &amp; AG/9.
            Open AG/3, AG/6 and AG/9 and vent the residual gas in the pipeline
            using vent stack and flame arrest. Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3 –
            Purging &amp; commissioning of mains).
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>
            Disconnect the suction inlet flange joint at Jeevan Auto, Parker Brother
            Auto CNG, Mastakar Auto, Oshiwara depot and SK Gajanan CNG Station
            compressors and positive isolation to be done. Re ensure closure of
            both stream inlet valve of DRS 12.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>8</td>
        <td>
            Close Valve V5.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>
            Issue Testing, Commissioning and Purging permit. Open Blind of Valve V2
            and connect the Nitrogen hose and start Nitrogen purging by opening
            valve V2 and venting from AG/3 &amp; AG/6 using a vent stack and flame
            arrestor. Refer: PTW System.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>
            Check % of gas at AG/3 &amp; AG/6 stop nitrogen purging when the level
            falls below the safe limit (Ensure – 0 PPM). <b>Refer COP: Section 08
            (Clause no. 3 – Purging &amp; commissioning of mains).</b>
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>11</td>
        <td>
            Issue hot and cold work permit, allow the construction team to cut
            the pipe at point ‘A’ &amp; point ‘B’.<b> Refer: PTW System.</b>
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>12</td>
        <td>
            Complete the Connectivity at Point A &amp; Point B with Existing
            Pipeline &amp; Newly laid pipeline.
        </td>
        <td>Contractor Team</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>
      <tr>
            <td>13</td>
            <td>
                Ensure quality of joints by reviewing NDT reports of the welds.
                <b> Refer COP: Section 52 (Clause No. 8 - NDT)</b>
            </td>
            <td>
                O&amp;M Engineer &amp;<br/>
                MGL QA Engineer &amp;<br/>
                NDT Agency
            </td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>14</td>
            <td>
                Check for any potential sources of ignition around valve
                AG/3, AG/6 and AG/9 and remove if any before venting.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td >15</td>
            <td >
                Close valve V2 &amp; put blind flange.
            </td>
            <td >O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td ></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td >16</td>
            <td >
                Issue Charging and commissioning permit and then open Valve V1 slowly
                and start venting from AG/3 and AG/6 by using vent stack and flame
                arrestor. (Refer: PTW System)
            </td>
            <td >O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td ></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>17</td>
            <td>
                Continue venting till 95% GIA is achieved at AG/3 &amp; AG/6
                and then close valve AG/3 &amp; AG/6 and put blind flange.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>18</td>
            <td>
                Re-connect compressor suction inlet flange joint of Jeevan Auto,
                Parker Brother Auto &amp; Mastakar Auto, Oshiwara Depot and
                SK Gajanan CNG Station compressors then open Valve V5 slowly and
                ensure 95% GIA achieved at inlet valve of compressor then open
                compressor inlet valve and restart compressor
                <b> (Refer: WI: O &amp; M WI 102)</b>
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>19</td>
            <td>
                Ensure 95% GIA achieved at inlet of DRS 12.
                Open both stream inlet valve and then take DRS 12 on-line.
                <b> (Refer: WI: O &amp; M WI 102)</b>
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td><td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>20</td>
            <td>
                Check all flanged joints for leakages with soap solution &amp; Gasoseeker.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>21</td>
            <td>
                Close all work permits and inform Emergency Control Room
                about the completion of NRO.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
</table>
